  "id": "Compound::DB01054 - Gene::776",
  "verbalization": "Nitrendipine is likely to interact with Cacna1d through a shared pathway involving high voltage-gated calcium channels. The evidence suggests that Nitrendipine binds to Cacna1s or Cacnb2, which are both involved in the same biological process—high voltage-gated calcium channel activity. This activity is then participated by Cacna1d, indicating a potential functional link between these proteins. The overlapping roles of Cacna1s and Cacnb2 in regulating calcium channels suggest that Nitrendipine may influence Cacna1d through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating calcium channel function. The integrated evidence implies that Nitrendipine's interaction with these channels could have a downstream effect on Cacna1d, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
